#~ msgstr "`.instui-avatar` · <span class=\"instui-pill -color-success pantoken-doc-tag\">stable</span> — Doeavttiravddáš avatar mii osohii vuolgit bokstavvut dahje bilda, rundejuvvon dahje default."

#, no-c-format
#~ msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
#~ msgid "By default the palette colour tints the initials on a transparent surface; `-has-inverse-color` fills the surface with the colour and puts the initials on-colour. The `-color-ai` variant always fills with the violet→sea gradient. For a full display name, put it in the content (so it stays in the accessibility tree) and add `data-initials=\"XX\"` for the compact visual — the real text is what a screen reader announces. Without `data-initials`, overflowing content just hard-clips (no ellipsis); wrap it in `.name` for a precise single-leading-letter clip instead, or split it into `.first-name`/`.last-name` for two clipped letters (either half can be omitted and the other stays centred)."
#~ msgstr "Defaultis palettas farge vuolga bokstavvuid transparenttalaš almmuheapmi; `-has-inverse-color` luftealmmuheapmi almmuheapmmaid fargain ja láhuvva bokstavvuid fargain. `-color-ai` -variantta luftealmmuheapmi aina violetta→mearkka gradienta. Giitu dutnje beaivvi njuolga birra, oahppa dadjat dat buot gisttumi (das dihtii leat accessibility -guovddáš) ja addit `data-initials=\"XX\"` compact visualiin — reala textta lea mii skjermlesára oahppá. Ilma `data-initials` giehtet barggut doarvái (ellipsiisalaš eai); bođá `.name` precise single-leading-letter clip -iin, dahje osádat siskkudas `.first-name`/`.last-name` dahje ožžon gaskavuođaid (juovllat fárrui olmmoš galggašat ja ođđa šatnalit galggai buresseamos)."

